Terrain (Wave 1) — the chat.go wiring, handed over as a note. NOT APPLIED.

Wave 1 of audit-notes/world-grounded-planning.md landed on branch `terrain-w1`:
`plan.RenderTerrain(dir, goal)` renders a deterministic, code-only snapshot of a
run's workspace; `plan.Options.Terrain` carries it onto `Graph.Terrain`, and
`graph.context()` renders it between the goal and the settled points. Empty
terrain emits zero bytes, so every prompt in a run without a workspace is byte
for byte the prompt it is today. Nothing below changes behaviour for a chat
session that does not opt in.

The campaign never edits cmd/aforge/chat.go while the chat rebuild owns it, so
the two `plan.Build` call sites are written down here instead of applied. Apply
whenever convenient — or not at all; the feature is complete without it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What the two lines are

  plan.Options{
      ...
      Terrain: plan.RenderTerrain(<workspace dir>, <goal>),
  }

at cmd/aforge/chat.go:5117 (planSubtree) and :5303 (replanRemainder), line
numbers as of the chat-v2 working tree on 2026-08-10.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why it is not literally two lines

There is no workspace variable in scope at either site. Both functions are
package-level and take (settings, planClient, workClient, plans, history); the
directory they would describe lives in `buildBrain` as `workspaceRoot`
(chat.go:302). So the wiring is one new parameter threaded down two call chains,
plus the two lines above.

Which directory to pass is the real decision, and the honest answer is: only a
shared workspace has anything true to show. In the default layout each job works
in `workspaceRoot/<jobID>`, created at dispatch — it does not exist when the plan
is built, and `workspaceRoot` itself holds only the other jobs' folders, which
says nothing about this goal and would spend prompt budget saying it. Under
`--shared-workspace` the root is the person's own material, which is exactly what
the planner is blind to today. Hence the `terrainRoot` below, empty by default.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. cmd/aforge/chat.go — buildBrain, just after workspaceRoot is settled (~305)

     if err := os.MkdirAll(workspaceRoot, 0o700); err != nil {
         return nil, brain.abandon(fmt.Errorf("create chat workspace: %w", err))
     }
+    // What the planner is allowed to see of the world before it plans. Only a
+    // shared workspace holds the person's own material; in the per-job layout
+    // the directory a job will work in does not exist yet, and the root above
+    // it holds nothing but the other jobs' folders. Empty renders nothing and
+    // every planning prompt stays exactly as it is.
+    terrainRoot := ""
+    if opts.sharedWorkspace {
+        terrainRoot = workspaceRoot
+    }

